FerrionOS change to the Redox kernel (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit e7f1d4231d0f4b55fbef229d9cd9459302c101f4 with ferrion-quiet-boot.patch, ferrion-boot-name.patch and ferrion-lockdown.patch applied:
- a read or fpath answered by a user-space scheme copies back from the head and tail bounce pages only the bytes the scheme reported, clamped to the request; the rest of the caller's buffer keeps its contents instead of being zeroed.

